-- ============================================================
-- Warrior (Protection): Anticipation
-- ============================================================
-- TODO.md: "Anticipation (2, 1): Increases your Dodge chance by 5%, and
--           dodging an attack increases the damage of your next attack by 10%.
--           (5 ranks)"
--
-- Both numbers in that line are the RANK 5 values, which is how the rest of the
-- Protection list is written.  The dodge half is therefore unchanged -- stock
-- Anticipation is already +1/2/3/4/5% (base points 0..4) -- and the new half
-- scales to match at 2/4/6/8/10%.
--
-- What the talent was.  Five ranks of flat dodge and nothing else: the purest
-- example of a talent you take because the tier demands five points, not
-- because you ever notice it.  Dodging is also the one defensive outcome that
-- pays a Protection warrior nothing -- parry at least advances the swing timer,
-- and block feeds Shield Slam and (now) Shield Mastery.  Giving dodge an
-- offensive payout puts it on the same footing as the Arms parry engine
-- (Small Victories, Riposte) without duplicating it.
--
-- Zero C++.  The talent gains SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL on its free
-- Effect2; spell_proc selects the dodge outcome; the buff is a plain
-- SPELL_AURA_ADD_PCT_MODIFIER with one charge, which the engine consumes on the
-- first cast that matches -- no proc row, no script.  See the "next spell"
-- consumption pattern in CLAUDE.md.
--
-- Why five buff spells rather than one.  The magnitude is per rank and
-- SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL casts the trigger with the TRIGGER's base
-- points, not the talent's, so each rank needs its own payload.  Same reason
-- Hobble needed 200620-200622.
--
-- Two details that are load-bearing on the buff:
--
--   SpellFamilyName = 4.  SpellInfo::IsAffectedBySpellMod ends in
--       IsAffected(affectSpell->SpellFamilyName, mod->mask) (SpellInfo.cpp:1359),
--       so a modifier whose family does not match the warrior's affects
--       nothing.  Anticipation itself is family 0, so this cannot be inherited
--       from the --base clone.
--
--   SpellClassMask A/B/C = -1 (0xFFFFFFFF).  "Your next attack" means any
--       warrior ability, so the mask is fully open.  Note this does NOT include
--       white swings: a spell modifier is only consulted for spells, which is
--       the accepted trade for keeping this pure DBC.
--
-- spell_proc: ProcFlags 40 = 0x28 = PROC_FLAG_TAKEN_MELEE_AUTO_ATTACK (0x8)
-- | PROC_FLAG_TAKEN_SPELL_MELEE_DMG_CLASS (0x20) -- the TAKEN side, since the
-- warrior is being attacked.  HitMask 16 = PROC_HIT_DODGE (SpellMgr.h:261).
-- SpellPhaseMask 2 is mandatory; a zero phase mask never fires and logs
-- nothing.  Chance 0 means "always" -- every dodge grants the buff.
--
-- Spells:
--   12297 / 12750 / 12751 / 12752 / 12753 = Anticipation ranks 1-5
--   200641 - 200645                       = Anticipation buff ranks 1-5 (new)
-- ============================================================

